# Line endings are a repository property, not a machine one.
#
# Without this file the LF content in the object store depends on each clone's `core.autocrlf`:
# Windows defaults it to true, so every checked-out file arrives CRLF while the blob stays LF.
# Nothing in this toolchain breaks on that, but it makes diffs noisy on a fresh clone and it means
# `dist/_headers` and `dist/_redirects` - which Cloudflare Pages parses verbatim - are byte-different
# per machine. Pinning `eol=lf` makes the checkout, the diff and the deployed payload identical
# everywhere, and it survives a teammate who has `core.autocrlf` set the other way.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never attempt a conversion on a payload that is not text, however git's heuristic reads it.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.gz binary
